---
const faqs = [
  {
    question:
      "What is the difference between logo design and brand identity?",
    answer:
      "A logo is one identifying element. Brand identity is the broader visual system that can include logo usage, colours, typography, graphic language and rules for applying the brand consistently.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can LKProfessionals redesign an existing brand?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Existing brands can be refined, refreshed or redesigned depending on what needs to change and what existing recognition should be preserved.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Do you provide the final logo and design files?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Final deliverables can include appropriate production and usage formats based on the agreed scope.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can branding and website design be handled together?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Coordinating identity and website work can help create a more consistent visual and user experience across the digital presence.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Is UI/UX design the same as graphic design?",
    answer:
      "No. UI/UX design focuses on how people understand and operate digital interfaces. Graphic design primarily handles visual communication across marketing, business and brand materials.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can you create ongoing marketing graphics after the brand is established?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Once the visual system exists, additional digital or print assets can be designed to remain consistent with the established identity.",
  },
];
---

<section class="brand-faq">
  <div class="site-container brand-faq__layout">
    <div>
      <p>Branding & design FAQ</p>

      <h2>
        Questions before defining the visual system.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="brand-faq__list">
      {
        faqs.map((faq) => (
          <details>
            <summary>{faq.question}</summary>
            <p>{faq.answer}</p>
          </details>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .brand-faq {
    padding-block: clamp(5rem, 10vw, 9rem);
    background: #ffffff;
  }

  .brand-faq__layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns:
      minmax(16rem, 0.68fr)
      minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(3rem, 9vw, 8rem);
  }

  .brand-faq__layout
    > div:first-child > p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: #0b2f8f;
    font-size: 0.64rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .brand-faq h2 {
    max-width: 11ch;
    margin: 0;
    color: #0d203c;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4.6rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.05em;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .brand-faq__list {
    border-top: 1px solid #dce3ec;
  }

  .brand-faq details {
    border-bottom: 1px solid #dce3ec;
    padding-block: 1rem;
  }

  .brand-faq summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    color: #293b53;
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    font-weight: 740;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .brand-faq details p {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
    color: #788497;
    font-size: 0.69rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  @media (max-width: 52rem) {
    .brand-faq__layout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
